{"title":"Career Roadmap: Studio Technician","role":"Studio Technician","summary":"A Studio Technician is responsible for preparing, operating, maintaining and troubleshooting the technical equipment used in photography, audio recording, video production, broadcasting, podcasts, live sessions and other studio environments.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (General / Honours)","Course":"Photography / Sound Engineering"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build technical expertise in studio equipment, audio/video systems, photography, lighting, recording and production workflows"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Studio Technician is responsible for preparing, operating, maintaining and troubleshooting the technical equipment used in photography, audio recording, video production, broadcasting, podcasts, live sessions and other studio environments."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the studio, the role may involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cameras"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Microphones"},{"text":"Audio consoles"},{"text":"Audio interfaces"},{"text":"Monitors"},{"text":"Recording systems"},{"text":"Video equipment"},{"text":"Cables and signal routing"},{"text":"Studio acoustics"},{"text":"Power and equipment safety"},{"text":"Editing and post-production support"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Studio Technology","Photography/Audio","Signal Flow","Equipment Operation","Troubleshooting","Digital Production"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Photography, audio and electronics fundamentals"},{"text":"Cameras, microphones, acoustics, basic electronics"},{"text":"Equipment-handling exercises"},{"text":"Only theoretical m